WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:12.709
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with this guy's name that is impossible to

00:00:12.709 --> 00:00:14.920
pronounce.

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:19.710
My name is Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér, and
indeed, it seems that pronouncing my name

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:22.270
requires some advanced technology.

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:23.960
So what was this?

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:28.730
I promise to tell you in a moment, but to
understand what happened here, first, let’s

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:32.870
have a look at this deepfake technique we
showcased a few videos ago.

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:38.590
As you see, we are at the point where our
mouth, head, and eye movements are also realistically

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:44.190
translated to a chosen target subject, and
perhaps the most remarkable part of this work

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:49.820
was that we don’t even need a video of this
target person, just one photograph.

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:55.960
However, these deepfake techniques mainly
help us in transferring video content.

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:58.640
So what about voice synthesis?

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:01.879
Is it also as advanced as this technique we’re
looking at?

00:01:01.879 --> 00:01:06.700
Well, let’s have a look at an example, and
you can decide for yourself.

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:12.250
This is a recent work that goes by the name
Tacotron 2, and it performs AI-based voice

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:13.430
cloning.

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:18.330
All this technique requires is a 5-second
sound sample of us, and is able to synthesize

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:22.910
new sentences in our voice, as if we uttered
these words ourselves.

00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:34.480
Let’s listen to a couple examples.

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:46.690
Wow, these are truly incredible.

00:01:46.690 --> 00:01:52.440
The timbre of the voice is very similar, and
it is able to synthesize sounds and consonants

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:57.170
that have to be inferred because they were
not heard in the original voice sample.

00:01:57.170 --> 00:02:03.220
And now, let’s jump to the next level, and
use a new technique that takes a sound sample

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:08.390
and animates the video footage as if the target
subject said it themselves.

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:13.980
This technique is called Neural Voice Puppetry,
and even though the voices here are synthesized

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:18.980
by this previous Tacotron 2 method that you
heard a moment ago, we shouldn’t judge this

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:31.720
technique by its audio quality, but how well
the video follows these given sounds.

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:46.200
Let’s go!

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:50.840
If you decide to stay until the end of this
video, there will be another fun video sample

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:52.320
waiting for you there.

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:57.760
Now, note that this is not the first technique
to achieve results like this, so I can’t

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:00.980
wait to look under the hood and see what’s
new here.

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:07.000
After processing the incoming audio, the gestures
are applied to an intermediate 3D model, which

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:13.220
is specific to each person since each speaker
has their own way of expressing themselves.

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:18.900
You can see this intermediate 3D model here,
but we are not done yet, we feed it through

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:24.990
a neural renderer, and what this does is apply
this motion to the particular face model shown

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:26.290
in the video.

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:32.280
You can imagine the intermediate 3D model
as a crude mask that models the gestures well,

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:37.910
but does not look like the face of anyone,
where the neural renderer adapts this mask

00:03:37.910 --> 00:03:39.810
to our target subject.

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:46.630
This includes adapting it to the current resolution,
lighting, face position and more, all of which

00:03:46.630 --> 00:03:49.910
is specific to what is seen in the video.

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:55.100
What is even cooler is that this neural rendering
part runs in real time.

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:58.050
So, what do we get from all this?

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:05.510
Well, one, superior quality, but at the same
time, it also generalizes to multiple targets.

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:19.000
Have a look here!

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:23.770
And the list of great news is not over yet,
you can try it yourself, the link is available

00:04:23.770 --> 00:04:25.380
in the video description.

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:27.130
Make sure to leave a comment with your results!

00:04:27.130 --> 00:04:32.600
To sum up, by combining multiple existing
techniques, it is important that everyone

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:38.210
knows about the fact that we can both perform
joint video and audio synthesis for a target

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:39.530
subject.

